right.code:
// bug: 1 + N queries
$posts = Post::all();
foreach ($posts as $post) echo $post->author->name;

// fix: 2 queries, any N
$posts = Post::with('author')->get();

// nested + constrained
$posts = Post::with(['author', 'comments' => fn($q) => $q->where('approved', true)->limit(5)])->get();

// fail loudly in dev (AppServiceProvider::boot)
Model::preventLazyLoading(!app()->isProduction());

// count without loading
Post::withCount('comments')->get();   // $post->comments_count

// already have the collection
$posts->load('author');

practice.task:
Fix this and explain the query count before/after:
$orders = Order::where('status','paid')->get();
foreach ($orders as $o) { echo $o->customer->name; echo $o->items->count(); }

practice.solution:
$orders = Order::where('status','paid')->with('customer')->withCount('items')->get();
foreach ($orders as $o) { echo $o->customer->name; echo $o->items_count; }

Before: 1 + N (customers) + N (items) = 2N+1 queries. After: 3 queries total, any N. withCount avoids loading every item row just to count.
